      "artist": "John Allan",
      "description": "Sabhal Mòr Ostaig, near to Kilmore, Skye, Highland, Scotland.\nColaiste Ghàidhlig na h-Alba.\nFounded in 1973, Sabhal Mòr Ostaig (The big barn at Ostaig) is an internationally recognised centre for the Gaelic language and culture. The college is a part of the University of the Highlands and Islands.\n\nCurrent student numbers are around 100 on full-time courses, about 160 on distance learning courses, and up to 900 on short courses each year.\n\nThese are recent buildings that have been added to the original 'big barn'. There is more significant building work underway for the next phase of expansion.\n\n\nÀrainn oideachaidh air leth.",
